              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 leading-relaxed pt-1">
                <strong>Interval for the calibrated estimate.</strong> There is no reliable closed-form interval here: the correction is a ratio of estimated
                coefficients from two models fitted in two samples. Run the bootstrap in the generated R code and paste the percentile bounds below —
                on the same scale as β̂ (log HR / log RR), not as a ratio. Left blank, the protocol reports a point estimate with no interval, which is the honest default.
              </p>
